<https://github.com/john1hsu/chess-graph/id/chunking-theory> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The theory, proposed by William Chase and Herbert Simon in 1973, that chess skill rests on a large store of familiar piece configurations (\"chunks\") held in long-term memory, which strong players recognise as single units and which cue relevant moves." .
