<https://github.com/john1hsu/chess-graph/id/isolated-queens-pawn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A pawn structure in which one side has a d-pawn with no friendly pawns on the c- and e-files; it gives its owner space, open files and central outposts in exchange for a static weakness that can be blockaded and attacked, especially as pieces come off." .
